From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: describe the
 SC8547D charge pumps (disabled)

The Pad 4 has two Southchip SC8547D 2:1 charge pumps for VOOC /
SuperVOOC and PPS charging. The stock device tree has the primary one,
which is also the VOOC / UFCS PHY, at 0x6a on qupv3_hub_i2c0 (our
i2c_hub_0) with its interrupt on gpio0, and the secondary one at 0x6a
on qupv3_se12_i2c (our i2c12) with its interrupt on gpio3; both buses
run at 400 kHz (qcom,clk-freq-out). Stock has no other device on
either bus. The interrupt pins are plain GPIO inputs with a pull-up and
2 mA drive (charging_inter_active / slave_charging_inter_active, the
same as the _sleep states); the vendor driver requests the interrupt
falling-edge triggered.

Describe both chips, their interrupts and pin states, and the bus rate.
Nothing changes at run time: both buses stay disabled, both chip nodes
are disabled and no driver binds to them, so none of the pins is muxed
or configured. gpio0, gpio3, gpio66 / gpio67 (i2c_hub_0) and
gpio208 / gpio209 (i2c12) are outside gpio-reserved-ranges. This is the
first step towards a charge-pump driver; a read-only identification
test enables the two buses through a test-only DTB.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 58 +
 1 file changed, 58 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1398,6 +1398,27 @@
 	drive-strength = <8>;
 };
 
+/*
+ * The secondary SC8547D 2:1 charge pump of the VOOC / SuperVOOC path (stock:
+ * sc8547-charger-slave@6A on qupv3_se12_i2c, 400 kHz, IRQ on gpio3). Only
+ * described: the bus stays disabled and no driver binds to the chip.
+ */
+&i2c12 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	sc8547d_secondary: charger@6a {
+		compatible = "southchip,sc8547d";
+		reg = <0x6a>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 3 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&cp_secondary_int_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+};
+
 &i2c14 {
 	status = "okay";
 
@@ -1421,6 +1442,27 @@
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The primary SC8547D 2:1 charge pump, also the VOOC / UFCS PHY (stock:
+ * oplus,sc8547d@6A on qupv3_hub_i2c0, 400 kHz, IRQ on gpio0). Only
+ * described: the bus stays disabled and no driver binds to the chip.
+ */
+&i2c_hub_0 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+	sc8547d_primary: charger@6a {
+		compatible = "southchip,sc8547d";
+		reg = <0x6a>;
+
+		interrupts-extended = <&tlmm 0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
+
+		pinctrl-0 = <&cp_primary_int_default>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+};
+
 &i2c_hub_1 {
 	/* the vendor I2C driver's default; the vendor tree sets no other rate for this bus */
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
@@ -2173,6 +2215,22 @@
 	/* stock's qcom,gpios-reserved: 36-43, 74, 119, 120, 144-147 */
 	gpio-reserved-ranges = <36 8>, <74 1>, <119 2>, <144 4>;
 
+	/* stock charging_inter_active (= _sleep): the primary SC8547D's interrupt */
+	cp_primary_int_default: cp-primary-int-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio0";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
+	/* stock slave_charging_inter_active (= _sleep): the secondary SC8547D's interrupt */
+	cp_secondary_int_default: cp-secondary-int-default-state {
+		pins = "gpio3";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
+
 	/* the pogo data line as a GPIO: low = a dock is attached and unpowered or asleep (stock uart_wake_gpio) */
 	pogo_detect_default: pogo-detect-default-state {
 		pins = "gpio151";
-- 
2.43.0

